0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, APRIL 16, 2008\r\rMayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r1. One matter of Anticipated Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section G.C. G.C. 54956.9b(3)(C), a point has been reached where, in the opinion of the City Council/Agency on the advice of its legal counsel, based on the below-described existing facts and circumstances, there is a significant exposure to litigation against the City Council/Agency: Receipt of Claim pursuant to Tort Claims Act or other written communication from Los Angeles Regional Water Quality Control Board Notice of Violation directed to Calabasas, Los Angeles County, and 19 other cities threatening litigation (copy available for public inspection in City Clerk�s office). \r2. Pending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a): Calabasas Ridge HOA v. Gordon, LC 079145; Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS 106644; Cooper v. Calabasas Park Estates Owners Association,�BC 323695; Toby Keeler & Elizabeth Stephens v. City of Calabasas, BS 109503; Parks v. City of Calabasas, BC 382012.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:23 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 7:33 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Glen Peterson.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, reported that there was no reportable action in closed session.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Mayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Maurer introduced Glen Peterson from Las Virgenes Water Management District, who presented books to the City from the District�s Annual Book Program and spoke regarding the District�s water situation. Councilmember Washburn announced that the Anza in Calabasas pageant will be held at the Gillette Ranch on April 27, 2008. He spoke regarding the recent Las Virgenes Council of Governments meeting and the Malibu Creek Watershed Run-off Conference. Councilmember Bozajian spoke regarding the upcoming Historical Tours and the upcoming Calabasas Fine Arts Festival. Mayor Maurer announced a Creek Clean-up that will be held in conjunction with �Big Sunday� on May 4, 2008.\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r \r Britt Aaronson, Calabasas, expressed her appreciation to the City for allowing her to be involved in the City�s processes while she was a resident of the City of Calabasas. Tom Ybarra, spoke regarding his company�s solid waste and recycling services.\r \rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the April 2, 2008 City Council meeting.\r\r Recommendation to award contract to Ortco, Inc. in the amount of $74,682.00 for the playground �poured-in-place� safety surfacing project at Juan Bautista de Anza Park,� Specification No. 07-08-013.\r\r Recommendation to accept completion of Freedom Drive Pavement Rehabilitation by Palp Inc. dba Excel Paving, Specification No. 07-08-04; and to direct the City Clerk to file the Notice of Completion.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1124, initiating proceedings for the levy and collection of assessments within Landscape and Lighting Districts Nos. 22, 24, 27 And 32 and ordering preparation of a Preliminary Engineer�s Report; and Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1125, approving Proposition 218 and the report of the engineer prepared for the levy and collection of assessments against the lots and parcels of property within the Landscape and Lighting Districts Nos. 22, 24, 27 and 32 for Fiscal Year 2008-2009; and Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1126, declaring its intent to levy and collect assessments within Landscape and Lighting Districts Nos. 22, 24, 27 and 32 and setting a time and place for public hearing.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1127, approving a policy for contributing to the funding of community services organizations and rescinding Resolution No. 2005-985.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1128, in support of a ban on secondhand smoke by the Los Angeles Board of Supervisors. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 with a revision to Item #1. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rPUBLIC HEARING \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2008-1123, to uphold the Planning Commission�s decision to approve Conditional Use Permit No. 700-002 and Oak Tree Permit No. 007-002 for the construction of a new single-family residence, pool, spa, driveway and associated fences and retaining walls located at 24226 Dry Canyon Cold Creek Road, within the HM zoning district and scenic corridor overlay zone.\r\r Mayor Maurer opened the public hearing.\r\r Michael Klein, Associate Planner, presented the staff report.\r\r Mehdi Amadi, Applicant, presented background information on his proposed project. Dale Vance, Calabasas, and Diane Johnson, Calabasas, Appellants, and Debra Collins, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the proposed project due to its incompatibility with the neighborhood. \r\rMayor Maurer closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2008-1123 to uphold the Planning Commission�s decision to approve Conditional Use Permit No. 700-002 and Oak Tree Permit No. 007-002 for the construction of a new single-family residence, pool, spa, driveway and associated fences and retaining walls located at 24226 Dry Canyon Cold Creek Road with the additional conditions when a public sewer is constructed within 250� of the project site, the applicant shall abandon the septic system; that the driveway shall be no wider than required by the Fire Department standards; and that appellant�s fees are waived. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Mayor Maurer voting no. \r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2008-246, amending Article X of Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code and adopting by reference the 2008 Consolidated Fire Protection District Code of the County of Los Angeles which amends Title 32 of the Los Angeles County Code and the California Fire Code, 2007 Edition.\r\r Mayor Maurer opened the public hearing.\r\r Sparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Maurer closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, to introduce Ordinance No. 2008-246 amending Article X of Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code and adopting by reference the 2008 Consolidated Fire Protection District Code of the County of Los Angeles which amends Title 32 of the Los Angeles County Code and the California Fire Code, 2007 Edition. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Discussion regarding sewer services expansion and management of citywide�septic systems.\r\rBob Woodward, Deputy City Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rIt was determined that Mayor pro Tem Wolfson had a conflict with discussing the recommendation on septic system inspections, therefore he recused himself and left the room. \r\rHal Helsley, Calabasas, Shelly Palmer, Calabasas, Randy Miller, Calabasas, Richard Windham, Calabasas, Maryellen Stroke, Calabasas, expressed concern over the proposed septic system inspection program. Mireille Newman, Calabasas, spoke in support of a carefully crafted septic system inspection program.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve staff�s recommendation to return to the City Council with an ordinance regarding a septic system inspection program. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor pro Tem Wolfson was absent due to his recusal.\r\rHal Helsley, Calabasas, Jody Thomas, Calabasas, Richard Windham, Calabasas, Pete Orteza, Calabasas, Mireille Newman, Calabasas, Randy Miller, Calabasas, Maryellen Stroke, Russ Sutherland, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the replacement of septic systems with sewer lines in the Old Topanga area.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to authorize staff to do a preliminary design and environmental review to investigate the potential of the proposed sewer services expansion project in the Old Topanga area. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Councilmember Bozajian voting no.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of March 24, 2008 to April 3, 2008.\r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\rMayor pro Tem Wolfson announced that the Civic Center Grand Opening will be held on July 13, 2008.\r\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\rCity Manager Coroalles indicated that there was nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\rCouncilmember Washburn requested that an item on water quality requirements in the City be placed on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN \r\r The City Council adjourned at 11:00 p.m. in memory of Steve DeSantis.\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r04/16/08\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0